# Tailwind 4 class names

Admin is Tailwind **v4**. Write the v4 canonical class. If the editor says `The class X can be written as Y`, use **Y** — do not leave the old form.

## CSS variables

Use parentheses, not `var()` or square-bracket `--` tokens:

```html
<!-- ❌ -->
<div class="max-w-[var(--ui-radius)] bg-[--color] w-[100%]" />

<!-- ✅ -->
<div class="max-w-(--ui-radius) bg-(--color) w-full" />
```

## Renamed utilities (v3 → v4)

| Do not use | Use instead |
| --- | --- |
| `shadow-sm` / `shadow` | `shadow-xs` / `shadow-sm` |
| `rounded-sm` / `rounded` | `rounded-xs` / `rounded-sm` |
| `blur-sm` / `blur` | `blur-xs` / `blur-sm` |
| `outline-none` | `outline-hidden` |
| `flex-shrink-0` / `flex-grow` | `shrink-0` / `grow` |
| `overflow-ellipsis` | `text-ellipsis` |
| `bg-black bg-opacity-50` | `bg-black/50` |

Prefer Nuxt UI tokens and existing `ui` slots over raw one-off v3 class strings.
